  title: Indian theatre
  text: Sanskrit drama flourished with Bhasa, Kalidasa and Bhavabhuti. Folk theatre includes Yakshagana, Jatra, Nautanki and Tamasha, and modern theatre grew with groups such as IPTA and institutions like the National School of Drama.
